&lt;p>It demonstrates how documentation can operate as a scalable product system.&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Knowledge Architecture Model</title><link>https://productnorth.in/platform-systems/knowledge-architecture/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><author>gdevika423@gmail.com (Devika Jallegowda)</author><guid>https://productnorth.in/platform-systems/knowledge-architecture/</guid><description>
&lt;hr class="page-divider">
&lt;p>I designed this knowledge architecture model to give the documentation team a shared structure for organizing and reusing information at scale.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>The knowledge architecture system is designed as a layered structure that connects how information is organized with how it is consumed and reused across workflows.&lt;/p>
&lt;br>
&lt;p align="center">
&lt;img src="https://productnorth.in/images/kb-scale.png" alt="Knowledge Architecture System Diagram" width="900">
&lt;/p>
&lt;p align="center">&lt;em>Figure: Knowledge Architecture System — Structure, Flow, and Execution&lt;/em>&lt;/p>
&lt;br>
&lt;h3>Taxonomy Structure&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="taxonomy-structure">&lt;/span>
&lt;a href="#taxonomy-structure" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section">&lt;/a>&lt;/h3>&lt;p>At the foundation is a structured taxonomy that organizes knowledge into clear categories.&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code">
